 sisterhood  had the goal of creating a super being  through careful manipulation of  bloodlines once they had achieved that  they would use this being who would be a  male possessing of all their powers and  more to manipulate the citizens of the  universe and shape the destiny of  mankind as they saw fit to make it  easier for the universe to accept their  being who they would call the quiz  that's had Iraq they set up false  prophecies on countless planets  throughout the empire prophecies which  would herald the coming of this being  the oppressed Freeman of the planet  Arrakis who had once been the son Sunni  Wanderers would have been prime  candidates for myth seeding if the  Sisterhood's plan had gone correctly  then they would have been able to wield  the strength of a super being but The  Sisterhood was never able to control  Paul once Paul is in the deep deserts of  Arrakis his powers are awakened by the  spice his prescient  eye begins to open and he starts to see  the full design of the Bene Jesuit plan  he also sees the path that will avenge  his father and restore the name of  tradies but it comes at a great cost  he knew the Fremen would call him God  Lisa and alga Eve the voice from the  outer world born of a bene Jesuit mother  as the prophecy foretold fanatics would  be created and the jihad of purification  would spread throughout the universe in  his name like a virus oppressing  countless worlds and costing the lives  of 60 billion humans the other path held  long patches of grey obscurity except  for peaks of violence he had seen a  warrior religion there a fire spreading  across the universe with the Atreides  green and black banner waving at the  head of fanatic legions drunk on spiced  liqueur guarentee Halleck and a few  others of his father's men a pitiful few  were among them all marked by the hawk  symbol from the shrine of his father's  skull  now let's be clear Paul did not want the  jihad to happen he doesn't fully  understand the visions and time itself  is not what it appears to be as later  the second points out in Children of  Dune the future forks in many potential  directions depending on what decisions  we make  Paul's prescient power however allows  him to see the future results of his  actions because of this he is able to  direct the path to become the fulcrum by  which fate turns upon throughout the  book Paul is haunted by visions of the  jihad he searches for a way to prevent  it but by then it has already gone too  far and in no path can he unsee it  surely I cannot choose that way he  thought but he saw it again in his  mind's eye the shrine of his father  skull and the violence with the green  and black banner waving in its midst  in the end Paul unseats the emperor and  restores the name of tradies but  something terrible has been set in  motion and in truth terrible things have  already been done on Arrakis the Fremen  had been manipulated into following a  man who allowed them to believe he was  God when he was not over the course of  the next 12 years the Fremen culture  withers and grades many of those who  follow Paul have now turned against him  the people of the Imperium begged for a  constitution but Paul rejects any  Constitution nothing may override his  power he allows nothing to limit his  Imperial will at this time all but a  fraction of the human universe existed  under Paul's rule Paul clings to his  empire out of fear of what is to come  hoping to save himself he knows that he  must act but doesn't even though he is  the only one who can I know this is  cliche but I really do have to quote  spider-man here with great power comes  great responsibility  Paul had seen the jihad too late and  failed to prevent the death of billions  of innocence but the jihad was a mere  fraction of what was to come  he remembered his earliest visions of  the jihad to be the terror and revulsion  he'd experienced now of course he knew  visions of greater terrors yet lived  with the real violence he had seen his  Freeman charged with mystical strength  sweep all before them in the religious  war the jihad gained a new perspective  it was finite of course a brief spasm  when measured against eternity but  beyond lay horrors to overshadow  anything in the past Paul knew that he  could stop it  he knew that he actually had a chance to  be the hero that he never really was to  save humanity from the horror that lay  in the darkness beyond he saw Crowley  sack the mythic battle at the end of  time but was unwilling to pay the  ultimate price to stop it he thought of  the jihad of the gene mingling across  parsecs and the vision which told him  how he might end it should he pay the  price all the hatefulness would  evaporate dying as fires die umber by  umber but oh the terrifying price I  never wanted to be a god he thought I  wanted only to disappear like a jewel of  trace do caught by the morning I wanted  to escape the Angels and the damned  alone as though by an oversight  the cost of what he must do in order to  save humanity haunts Paul throughout the  second book but ultimately he makes his  decision he puts himself before humanity  pushing the task of fixing the damage he  had done and preventing the ultimate  extinction of humankind on to his son  late to the second who would undergo  3,500 years of agony in his father's  place Paul saw the horrors of the golden  path which would ensure human survival  he saw the cruelty of it and he saw  Crowley's ech he weighed them against  each other but was unable to make the  decision unable to lock humankind into  the correct path Paul son Leto calls him  out on this when they finally meet at  the end of the book children of doom it  is sad that you were never really  Freeman later said we Freeman know how  to Commission the aretha our judges can  choose between evils it has always been  that way for us the curious thing about  Children of Dune is that late to the  second inherits the sins of his father  and he knows that it is up to him to do  what his father failed to do but in  order to do this he must move beyond his  humanity and become a true God and  prepare mankind for what is to come  though he knew he would never be thanked  for it theoretically it did not have to  be Leto who took on this burden his twin  sister Janina could have also taken his  place but he chose to spare her that  agony  Paul is the hero of the book dune in the  sense that he is the hero of his own arc  he gained her fins for his house and  becomes Emperor but he is not the hero  of the dune saga when the series as a  whole is considered Paul is not only  incapable of fixing the mess he made  once he sees a bigger mess in the future  that only he can stop he doesn't really  try he just gives up I know this is  quite the deflating resolution after the  epic ending of the first book and I  assure you this is intentional Frank  Herbert wants the reader to see the fal  ability of Paul to see that he is just a  man and always was regardless of what  powers he seems to possess it all goes  back to the key theme of dune which I  discussed in my video titled what's the  point of doom don't blindly follow  behind leaders always question alright  guys so this concisely as I can put it  is the reason why I think that Paul is  not meant to be viewed as the hero of  the day saga thank you guys so much for  watching please subscribe for more dnews  and as always with the new denis  villeneuve dude movie come  this year's starting team with a child  May we will be seeing more and more dune  movie news as the months go on and on  and I will be covering it all here on  this channel so please make sure you  like and subscribe let's hope that Paul  Atreides is portrayed accurately on the  big screen thank you guys so much for  watching  [Music]  special shout-out to my top patrons  Trini girl  Joseph Rosner Milton Christopher Appling  Richard Hess Deus Technica Giuliana  aaliyan the Collier report Pau